# Paths under services/rtvi/rt-cv/ that are NOT built into the vss-rt-cv image.
#
# docker/Dockerfile uses selective COPY: only src/ (the app sources + Makefile)
# and tests/ enter the container. Everything listed here never does, so changing
# it must NOT flip the "Check vss-rt-cv tag source" container-source check.
#
# Format: gitignore-style, paths relative to services/rtvi/rt-cv/. Used by
# .github/scripts/check_container_tag_source.py to decide whether a folder
# tree-SHA difference is source-relevant.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   src/     - compiled into the binary.
#   tests/   - COPYd into the image by docker/Dockerfile.
#   docker/  - not shipped, but it IS a build input: a Dockerfile change really
#              does make an existing image stale, so it must keep flipping the
#              check.
#
# configs/ is bind-mounted by the compose services at runtime rather than baked
# in, so a config edit cannot make the built image stale.
configs/
README.md
LICENSE.3rdparty
.ignore_source_code_check
